course: dictionary
lesson: 11669
title: Judging words: assessor
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An assessor is a person whose job is to judge or measure something. Read the words around the word: «The insurance assessor looked at the flooded kitchen and wrote down the damage.» Who looks at damage and writes it down? That tells you an assessor judges how bad something is.
explain: «Our teacher is an assessor, so she checks and marks the exams.» In school, an assessor is someone who checks and marks work. The clue is the word checks: an assessor looks closely and decides how good something is.
explain: Some words belong to a special area, like money. «The assessor worked out how much tax was due» is about money, so here an assessor is an official who works out the amount. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: An assessor is a person whose job is to judge or measure how good, big or valuable something is.
fact: «Assessor» can mean someone who checks and marks exams or coursework.
fact: «Assessor» can also mean an official who works out how much tax or insurance money is due.
fact: A loss assessor checks damage after a flood or fire, so the insurance company knows what to pay.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence: «The assessor measured the cracks in the wall» still makes sense if an assessor is someone who judges or measures.
exercise: «The insurance assessor looked at the flooded kitchen.» What is the assessor's job here? | A person who cooks food for the family | *A person whose job is to judge the damage | A bucket for collecting water | A small boat for the flood
exercise: «Our teacher is an assessor, so she checks and marks the exams.» What does an assessor do in this sentence? | Grows vegetables in the garden | *Checks and marks the exams | Sells sweets in the playground | Drives the school bus
exercise: «The assessor worked out how much tax was due.» Which word in this sentence tells you the assessor works with money? | *tax | assessor | worked | sentence
test: «The assessor measured the cracks in the wall and wrote a report.» What is the assessor doing here? | *Measuring the damage and judging it | Breaking the wall down | Building a new house | Painting the walls
test: Leo says an assessor is only a kind of teacher. Is he right? | No, an assessor is a type of bird | Yes, an assessor always sells houses | Yes, every assessor works in a school | *No, an assessor can also judge damage or work out money, not just mark exams
exam: Which best describes an assessor? | A person who only sells houses | A type of school bag | A loud noise made by a machine | *A person whose job is to judge or measure how good, big or valuable something is
